[{:db/id 17592186105847 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-828244f0-37d1-5218-b4cd-65ea8c882592"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-828244f0-37d1-5218-b4cd-65ea8c882592" :question/id #uuid "828244f0-37d1-5218-b4cd-65ea8c882592" :question/math-academy-id "q-95329" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{2x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $g(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={sinh}^{2}⁡x$ and $v(x)=2x+1.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({sinh}^{2}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot (2x+1)-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot (2x+1)^{′}}{(2x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\cdot (2x+1)-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot (2)}{(2x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2x+1)\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{(2x+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5cfa9a94-c719-5199-ba06-985601fc058f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5cfa9a94-c719-5199-ba06-985601fc058f" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfa9a94-c719-5199-ba06-985601fc058f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da810825-b5ef-5b80-8415-5e95017d7de5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3d646eb-777f-5cfa-a5f5-fbdbfeb38a97" "answer-da810825-b5ef-5b80-8415-5e95017d7de5" "answer-96918186-4f3f-5672-8772-478e2533d76d" "answer-560e7f3e-0d28-5092-9dc8-f284fb849140" "answer-ca7a5e34-b197-57ec-bafb-007ac6b6c167"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3d646eb-777f-5cfa-a5f5-fbdbfeb38a97" :answer/id #uuid "a3d646eb-777f-5cfa-a5f5-fbdbfeb38a97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1){sinh}^{2}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{4}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da810825-b5ef-5b80-8415-5e95017d7de5" :answer/id #uuid "da810825-b5ef-5b80-8415-5e95017d7de5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(2x+1)\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{(2x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96918186-4f3f-5672-8772-478e2533d76d" :answer/id #uuid "96918186-4f3f-5672-8772-478e2533d76d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-560e7f3e-0d28-5092-9dc8-f284fb849140" :answer/id #uuid "560e7f3e-0d28-5092-9dc8-f284fb849140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+(2x+1){sinh}^{2}⁡x}{(2x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca7a5e34-b197-57ec-bafb-007ac6b6c167" :answer/id #uuid "ca7a5e34-b197-57ec-bafb-007ac6b6c167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{4}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234079 :question/problem "Anna decides to go jogging. Her position from the starting point, measured in meters, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $14$ | $25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=7$ using a central difference approximation with the step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=7$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(7) & ≈\\frac{s(7+2)-s(7-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(9)-s(5)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{14-4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the velocity of Anna at the instant of time $t=7$ is $2.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-60159877-402e-50a4-b5a2-d2689fd74444"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60159877-402e-50a4-b5a2-d2689fd74444" :answer-field/id #uuid "60159877-402e-50a4-b5a2-d2689fd74444" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b12c9f3-2819-529b-8837-45ccdf607dd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0689c971-937c-53b8-b250-4c733f3231e7" "answer-2b12c9f3-2819-529b-8837-45ccdf607dd5" "answer-acddc305-2667-5de3-9e0a-d50c79f03f6a" "answer-b279ea53-ddd1-5ef6-943b-3673f2d4a39a" "answer-f9efdb0d-9921-564c-9406-de62171a83e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0689c971-937c-53b8-b250-4c733f3231e7" :answer/id #uuid "0689c971-937c-53b8-b250-4c733f3231e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b12c9f3-2819-529b-8837-45ccdf607dd5" :answer/id #uuid "2b12c9f3-2819-529b-8837-45ccdf607dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acddc305-2667-5de3-9e0a-d50c79f03f6a" :answer/id #uuid "acddc305-2667-5de3-9e0a-d50c79f03f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b279ea53-ddd1-5ef6-943b-3673f2d4a39a" :answer/id #uuid "b279ea53-ddd1-5ef6-943b-3673f2d4a39a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9efdb0d-9921-564c-9406-de62171a83e2" :answer/id #uuid "f9efdb0d-9921-564c-9406-de62171a83e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233097 :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3x-2}{4-{x}^{2}},$ which of the following statements is correct?\n\nI. ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=-\\infty $\n\nII. ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)=\\infty $\n\nIII. ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty $" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9482b22c-5636-533b-a174-f50d48546d41"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9482b22c-5636-533b-a174-f50d48546d41" :answer-field/id #uuid "9482b22c-5636-533b-a174-f50d48546d41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-920a8dbd-27b3-5123-881e-16a876ff9404" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d635a92-3fd4-5667-81aa-6078f06bd72a" "answer-920a8dbd-27b3-5123-881e-16a876ff9404" "answer-e0a063b0-76fe-550d-ae01-e8af9d24fad6" "answer-b986b8c3-93d6-5446-a4fe-c87752d0477c" "answer-df597881-80e1-518d-bee5-53858adff232"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d635a92-3fd4-5667-81aa-6078f06bd72a" :answer/id #uuid "1d635a92-3fd4-5667-81aa-6078f06bd72a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-920a8dbd-27b3-5123-881e-16a876ff9404" :answer/id #uuid "920a8dbd-27b3-5123-881e-16a876ff9404" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0a063b0-76fe-550d-ae01-e8af9d24fad6" :answer/id #uuid "e0a063b0-76fe-550d-ae01-e8af9d24fad6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b986b8c3-93d6-5446-a4fe-c87752d0477c" :answer/id #uuid "b986b8c3-93d6-5446-a4fe-c87752d0477c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df597881-80e1-518d-bee5-53858adff232" :answer/id #uuid "df597881-80e1-518d-bee5-53858adff232" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092309 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-28cd517a-376e-5db1-863f-bc38045c2ab7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-28cd517a-376e-5db1-863f-bc38045c2ab7" :question/id #uuid "28cd517a-376e-5db1-863f-bc38045c2ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-138921" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definition into the equation $4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})) & =-3 \\\\ 2({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =-3 \\\\ 2{e}^{x}-2{e}^{-x} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (2{e}^{x}-2{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (-3) \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}-2 & =-3{e}^{x} \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{x}-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in ${e}^{x}$ that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{e}^{x}-1)({e}^{x}+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n2{e}^{x}-1=0,\\,{e}^{x}+2=0\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{x}-1 & =0 &  & \\, & {e}^{x}+2 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{2} &  & \\, & {e}^{x} & =-2 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) &  & \\, & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no real values of $x$ for which ${e}^{x}=-2.$ Therefore, $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})$ is the only real solution to the equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a59f508-2043-5fd3-9b05-0601035dc322"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a59f508-2043-5fd3-9b05-0601035dc322" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a59f508-2043-5fd3-9b05-0601035dc322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c9a8d86-2ffd-5e45-8af5-dbc5542af39b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-90c9d555-99b8-53e3-88c7-b225b4935425" "answer-0c9a8d86-2ffd-5e45-8af5-dbc5542af39b" "answer-d9a928d8-001f-5b4e-b2db-218ec5e4289a" "answer-b0cc92cf-53cb-5cf1-a4fe-3b86e44133f5" "answer-fbdd1915-0f33-5496-97c5-b477aee6adf6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c9d555-99b8-53e3-88c7-b225b4935425" :answer/id #uuid "90c9d555-99b8-53e3-88c7-b225b4935425" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c9a8d86-2ffd-5e45-8af5-dbc5542af39b" :answer/id #uuid "0c9a8d86-2ffd-5e45-8af5-dbc5542af39b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9a928d8-001f-5b4e-b2db-218ec5e4289a" :answer/id #uuid "d9a928d8-001f-5b4e-b2db-218ec5e4289a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0cc92cf-53cb-5cf1-a4fe-3b86e44133f5" :answer/id #uuid "b0cc92cf-53cb-5cf1-a4fe-3b86e44133f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdd1915-0f33-5496-97c5-b477aee6adf6" :answer/id #uuid "fbdd1915-0f33-5496-97c5-b477aee6adf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233510 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\,1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/9d/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5109d536-d5f1-5dc6-99e6-dbfe65babe4c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5109d536-d5f1-5dc6-99e6-dbfe65babe4c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5109d536-d5f1-5dc6-99e6-dbfe65babe4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39083e26-3ab5-5681-8437-cc9ab5ac6173" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39083e26-3ab5-5681-8437-cc9ab5ac6173" "answer-9f14e973-894a-5a1a-8675-1eeeec064de6" "answer-02a1370b-1edb-5c5a-a24f-eaa2993f5356" "answer-afd60b49-163e-5f97-8d94-74dba8c40864" "answer-21bd116c-2d24-5d0e-ba67-f4580b818141"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39083e26-3ab5-5681-8437-cc9ab5ac6173" :answer/id #uuid "39083e26-3ab5-5681-8437-cc9ab5ac6173" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f14e973-894a-5a1a-8675-1eeeec064de6" :answer/id #uuid "9f14e973-894a-5a1a-8675-1eeeec064de6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02a1370b-1edb-5c5a-a24f-eaa2993f5356" :answer/id #uuid "02a1370b-1edb-5c5a-a24f-eaa2993f5356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afd60b49-163e-5f97-8d94-74dba8c40864" :answer/id #uuid "afd60b49-163e-5f97-8d94-74dba8c40864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21bd116c-2d24-5d0e-ba67-f4580b818141" :answer/id #uuid "21bd116c-2d24-5d0e-ba67-f4580b818141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176022 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-55d1a1bd-c8eb-5ee7-88d6-a44ae7dc2c96"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-55d1a1bd-c8eb-5ee7-88d6-a44ae7dc2c96" :question/id #uuid "55d1a1bd-c8eb-5ee7-88d6-a44ae7dc2c96" :question/math-academy-id "q-118710" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{x}{x-1})}^{3x-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that as $x\\to \\infty ,$ \n\n- the expression inside the parentheses approaches $1,$ while\n\n- the exponent approaches $\\infty .$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{x}{x-1})}^{3x-3}={1}^{\\infty },\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}=e\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{x}{x-1})}^{3x-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{(x-1)+1}{x-1})}^{3x-3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{x-1})}^{3(x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $x-1=n.$ Therefore, since $n\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we rewrite the limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{x}{x-1})}^{3x-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{x-1})}^{3(x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{3n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{n})}^{n}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c41454b8-a54a-5924-9bf1-be03ac5b4d5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c41454b8-a54a-5924-9bf1-be03ac5b4d5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c41454b8-a54a-5924-9bf1-be03ac5b4d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1c13605-3b15-5441-9ad6-991d71ce870e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4bc45995-cc23-5f2f-95dc-adb53fd70390" "answer-9b48a15c-7746-52d0-ab31-148949b28472" "answer-7d02c22e-415b-580d-b404-ffc0a846300a" "answer-a689aded-b802-5144-9786-711cd58ea390" "answer-b1c13605-3b15-5441-9ad6-991d71ce870e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bc45995-cc23-5f2f-95dc-adb53fd70390" :answer/id #uuid "4bc45995-cc23-5f2f-95dc-adb53fd70390" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b48a15c-7746-52d0-ab31-148949b28472" :answer/id #uuid "9b48a