eld/choices ["answer-4680a870-34ad-5604-97ab-11765b3e31ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4680a870-34ad-5604-97ab-11765b3e31ad" :answer/id #uuid "4680a870-34ad-5604-97ab-11765b3e31ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-24214f4f-5b69-59e3-9894-848806975f44" :question/id #uuid "24214f4f-5b69-59e3-9894-848806975f44" :question/math-academy-id "q-60890" :question/problem "What is the root of the function $f(x)=3x-6?$" :question/worked-solution "The roots are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ 3x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66e3b7da-db59-5f84-8105-1a853d4929a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66e3b7da-db59-5f84-8105-1a853d4929a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "66e3b7da-db59-5f84-8105-1a853d4929a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e679bf99-ebbd-59a6-be49-debbd1010a4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2794ce87-a947-5108-b8fa-e985c689ef9f" "answer-e679bf99-ebbd-59a6-be49-debbd1010a4e" "answer-dfd37043-455c-564e-842e-409d3f7027aa" "answer-9913eeb0-1120-5758-b6e8-0e0b303b40b6" "answer-6548fce5-29eb-52c1-a26c-7408d0d52849"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2794ce87-a947-5108-b8fa-e985c689ef9f" :answer/id #uuid "2794ce87-a947-5108-b8fa-e985c689ef9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e679bf99-ebbd-59a6-be49-debbd1010a4e" :answer/id #uuid "e679bf99-ebbd-59a6-be49-debbd1010a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfd37043-455c-564e-842e-409d3f7027aa" :answer/id #uuid "dfd37043-455c-564e-842e-409d3f7027aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9913eeb0-1120-5758-b6e8-0e0b303b40b6" :answer/id #uuid "9913eeb0-1120-5758-b6e8-0e0b303b40b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6548fce5-29eb-52c1-a26c-7408d0d52849" :answer/id #uuid "6548fce5-29eb-52c1-a26c-7408d0d52849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129816 :question/problem "What is the root of the function $g(x)=\\frac{x}{2}+4?$" :question/worked-solution "The roots are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-4 \\\\ x & =2(-4) \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128377 :answer-field/correct 17592186128380 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-093b2e5c-e9f3-501b-a863-23c715264f2d" :question/id #uuid "093b2e5c-e9f3-501b-a863-23c715264f2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-217139" :question/problem "The root of the function $g(x)=\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{x}{15}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The roots are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{x}{15} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{15} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{60}{3} \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=20.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-199bb04c-707f-598c-9a58-4c6728116832"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-199bb04c-707f-598c-9a58-4c6728116832" :answer-field/id #uuid "199bb04c-707f-598c-9a58-4c6728116832" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ebe89775-843f-5437-a1df-cab2ad77297f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ebe89775-843f-5437-a1df-cab2ad77297f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebe89775-843f-5437-a1df-cab2ad77297f" :answer/id #uuid "ebe89775-843f-5437-a1df-cab2ad77297f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b18fe87-24b2-577e-8e31-abad021a59b4" :question/id #uuid "6b18fe87-24b2-577e-8e31-abad021a59b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-82680" :question/problem "What is the root of the function $f(x)=1-4x?$" :question/worked-solution "The roots are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ 1-4x & =0 \\\\ 4x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e12e5f7b-b6de-5d51-928d-782cfbd15054"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e12e5f7b-b6de-5d51-928d-782cfbd15054" :answer-field/id #uuid "e12e5f7b-b6de-5d51-928d-782cfbd15054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2bd1505-96d6-5aae-b69d-971f69c4a205" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b26ce88b-4234-5e07-8be1-b8af7f56ff8d" "answer-77274b81-ef22-59bd-9661-11555500d02a" "answer-8b3a7994-4969-5df7-9fcc-644c20f5ea08" "answer-2581405a-b8c0-5f79-98e1-99d8680c6371" "answer-f2bd1505-96d6-5aae-b69d-971f69c4a205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b26ce88b-4234-5e07-8be1-b8af7f56ff8d" :answer/id #uuid "b26ce88b-4234-5e07-8be1-b8af7f56ff8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77274b81-ef22-59bd-9661-11555500d02a" :answer/id #uuid "77274b81-ef22-59bd-9661-11555500d02a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b3a7994-4969-5df7-9fcc-644c20f5ea08" :answer/id #uuid "8b3a7994-4969-5df7-9fcc-644c20f5ea08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2581405a-b8c0-5f79-98e1-99d8680c6371" :answer/id #uuid "2581405a-b8c0-5f79-98e1-99d8680c6371" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2bd1505-96d6-5aae-b69d-971f69c4a205" :answer/id #uuid "f2bd1505-96d6-5aae-b69d-971f69c4a205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130482 :tutorial/content "The **roots** of a function are the values of the input $x$ for which the function equals zero. For this reason, roots are sometimes also called **zeros**.\n\nAlgebraically, the roots of a function are the solutions for $x$ in the following equation:\n\n$$\nf(x)=0\n$$\n\nFor example, if $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{2}x+1,$ then we can find the roots by solving the equation $f(x) = 0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+1 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, this function has a single root: $x=-2.$\n\nGraphically, the roots of a function are the $x$-intercepts. For example, for the graph of $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{2}x+1$ shown below, we can see that the function intercepts the $x$-axis at $x=-2.$\n\n![](images/a7/a75e8a0ae40c5cc940f9fe2d9194b0dcb5c6db2742e87a6d903dc15c0b970e99.png)\n\nWhen shown on a graph, the roots of a function are also called the $\\boldsymbol x$**-intercepts.**" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129364 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100806 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d6a9fa51-d96f-5308-9675-af7e9df7f105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6a9fa51-d96f-5308-9675-af7e9df7f105" :question/id #uuid "d6a9fa51-d96f-5308-9675-af7e9df7f105" :question/math-academy-id "q-3563" :question/problem "Find, in ascending powers of $y,$ the first three terms of the binomial expansion of ${(10y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=5,$ $a=10y,$ and $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{5}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{4}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{3}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{3},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{4},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{5}.\n$$\n\nThe $5$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,5,10,10,5,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(10y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{5} & =1{a}^{5}+5{a}^{4}b+10{a}^{3}{b}^{2}+10{a}^{2}{b}^{3}+5a{b}^{4}+1{b}^{5} \\\\  & =1(10y)^{5}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{0}+5(10y)^{4}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{1}+10(10y)^{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & \\,+10(10y)^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}+5(10y)^{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4}+1(10y)^{0}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5} \\\\  & =1(100\\,000{y}^{5})(1)+5(10\\,000{y}^{4})(\\frac{1}{2})+10(1\\,000{y}^{3})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & \\,+10(100{y}^{2})(\\frac{1}{8})+5(10y)(\\frac{1}{16})+1(1)(\\frac{1}{32}) \\\\  & =100\\,000{y}^{5}+\\frac{50\\,000{y}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{10\\,000{y}^{3}}{4}+\\frac{1\\,000{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{50y}{16}+\\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =100\\,000{y}^{5}+25\\,000{y}^{4}+2\\,500{y}^{3}+125{y}^{2}+\\frac{25y}{8}+\\frac{1}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in ascending powers of $y$, the first three terms are\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{8}+125{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef1b5443-9d42-51aa-ac69-73ecc6958d74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef1b5443-9d42-51aa-ac69-73ecc6958d74" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef1b5443-9d42-51aa-ac69-73ecc6958d74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b600bcd-5006-5baf-9dca-4aab5033031d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5135b701-cd58-5dde-8d9b-989995318cb4" "answer-4c839c43-5c26-510d-85ac-e2e3c39a216c" "answer-0b600bcd-5006-5baf-9dca-4aab5033031d" "answer-9799692b-0119-5014-ae4f-3ef5e9145c63" "answer-4fb998d5-d716-53e2-a50b-72e1271eb277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5135b701-cd58-5dde-8d9b-989995318cb4" :answer/id #uuid "5135b701-cd58-5dde-8d9b-989995318cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{4}+100{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c839c43-5c26-510d-85ac-e2e3c39a216c" :answer/id #uuid "4c839c43-5c26-510d-85ac-e2e3c39a216c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{4}+145{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b600bcd-5006-5baf-9dca-4aab5033031d" :answer/id #uuid "0b600bcd-5006-5baf-9dca-4aab5033031d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{8}+125{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9799692b-0119-5014-ae4f-3ef5e9145c63" :answer/id #uuid "9799692b-0119-5014-ae4f-3ef5e9145c63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{8}+145{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fb998d5-d716-53e2-a50b-72e1271eb277" :answer/id #uuid "4fb998d5-d716-53e2-a50b-72e1271eb277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}+\\frac{25y}{8}-100{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ab532852-8985-56d4-9487-9412ea181516" "question-c989ddc2-999c-5079-ab1b-dc05c9512624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab532852-8985-56d4-9487-9412ea181516" :question/id #uuid "ab532852-8985-56d4-9487-9412ea181516" :question/math-academy-id "q-3564" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n{(2{t}^{2}-3s)}^{4}=A{t}^{8}+B{t}^{6}s+C{t}^{4}{s}^{2}-216{t}^{2}{s}^{3}+81{s}^{4}\n$$\n\nwhere $A,B$ and $C$ are constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=4,$ $a=2{t}^{2},$ and $b=-3s.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{4}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{3}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{3},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{2}-3s)^{4} & =1{a}^{4}+4{a}^{3}b+6{a}^{2}{b}^{2}+4a{b}^{3}+1{b}^{4} \\\\  & =1{(2{t}^{2})}^{4}(-3s)^{0}+4{(2{t}^{2})}^{3}(-3s)^{1}+6{(2{t}^{2})}^{2}(-3s)^{2} \\\\  & \\,+4{(2{t}^{2})}^{1}(-3s)^{3}+1{(2{t}^{2})}^{0}(-3s)^{4} \\\\  & =1(16{t}^{8})(1)+4(8{t}^{6})(-3s)+6(4{t}^{4})(9{s}^{2}) \\\\  & \\,+4(2{t}^{2})(-27{s}^{3})+1(1)(81{s}^{4}) \\\\  & =16{t}^{8}-96{t}^{6}s+216{t}^{4}{s}^{2}-216{t}^{2}{s}^{3}+81{s}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=16,B=-96,$ and $C=216.$ Finally,\n\n$$\nA+B+C=16-96+216=136.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-056e7899-7359-5aa3-9d75-0e24b35490d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-056e7899-7359-5aa3-9d75-0e24b35490d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "056e7899-7359-5aa3-9d75-0e24b35490d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ad5cbb7-83ea-5127-9a88-0dafeb6f2337" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eddbbe69-969c-5b54-965b-bba69c119ec3" "answer-3ad5cbb7-83ea-5127-9a88-0dafeb6f2337" "answer-6adb48dc-a33c-5da7-ae77-576efafa9e3f" "answer-83db7d2e-5441-54f0-9b72-b23bdd133079" "answer-1e0b8e5d-ea62-586b-acf8-47c7448fb9eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eddbbe69-969c-5b54-965b-bba69c119ec3" :answer/id #uuid "eddbbe69-969c-5b54-965b-bba69c119ec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ad5cbb7-83ea-5127-9a88-0dafeb6f2337" :answer/id #uuid "3ad5cbb7-83ea-5127-9a88-0dafeb6f2337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "136" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6adb48dc-a33c-5da7-ae77-576efafa9e3f" :answer/id #uuid "6adb48dc-a33c-5da7-ae77-576efafa9e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "168" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83db7d2e-5441-54f0-9b72-b23bdd133079" :answer/id #uuid "83db7d2e-5441-54f0-9b72-b23bdd133079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "320" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e0b8e5d-ea62-586b-acf8-47c7448fb9eb" :answer/id #uuid "1e0b8e5d-ea62-586b-acf8-47c7448fb9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "328" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c989ddc2-999c-5079-ab1b-dc05c9512624" :question/id #uuid "c989ddc2-999c-5079-ab1b-dc05c9512624" :question/math-academy-id "q-12884" :question/problem "Find, in descending powers of $y$ and ascending powers of $x,$ the first three terms of the binomial expansion of ${(y-x)}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=3,$ $a=y,$ and $b=-x.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,3,3,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(y-x)}^{3} & =1{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}b+3a{b}^{2}+1{b}^{3} \\\\  & =1(y)^{3}(-x)^{0}+3(y)^{2}(-x)^{1}+3(y)^{1}(-x)^{2}+1(y)^{0}(-x)^{3} \\\\  & =1({y}^{3})(1)+3({y}^{2})(-x)+3(y)({x}^{2})+1(1)(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & ={y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x+3y{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in descending powers of $y$ and ascending powers of $x,$ the first three terms are\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x+3y{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b892af4-e657-5e7b-967c-44dc67970e0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b892af4-e657-5e7b-967c-44dc67970e0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b892af4-e657-5e7b-967c-44dc67970e0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24ced81d-498a-516a-95d5-fb01dede7a9c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24ced81d-498a-516a-95d5-fb01dede7a9c" "answer-0bac5b62-4ee8-545a-966d-5c12ee806664" "answer-5e2cc4e3-3a7b-5190-9ba6-ed8c80cfcd59" "answer-6331dd90-d13b-5bdb-bc74-b83aa99db890" "answer-c137176e-2ac9-58c5-84bd-949dafa76422"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24ced81d-498a-516a-95d5-fb01dede7a9c" :answer/id #uuid "24ced81d-498a-516a-95d5-fb01dede7a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x+3y{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bac5b62-4ee8-545a-966d-5c12ee806664" :answer/id #uuid "0bac5b62-4ee8-545a-966d-5c12ee806664" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x-10y{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e2cc4e3-3a7b-5190-9ba6-ed8c80cfcd59" :answer/id #uuid "5e2cc4e3-3a7b-5190-9ba6-ed8c80cfcd59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x-6y{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6331dd90-d13b-5bdb-bc74-b83aa99db890" :answer/id #uuid "6331dd90-d13b-5bdb-bc74-b83aa99db890" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}-4{y}^{2}x+10y{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c137176e-2ac9-58c5-84bd-949dafa76422" :answer/id #uuid "c137176e-2ac9-58c5-84bd-949dafa76422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}-4{y}^{2}x+6y{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9b7f87c5-a873-5d35-a338-1eb6f31f95ee" :activity/id #uuid "9b7f87c5-a873-5d35-a338-1eb6f31f95ee" :activity/title "Expanding Binomials Using Pascal's Triangle" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048677 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-8cc0e099-5714-599b-80b4-eb693886b0be" "step-0fcd4859-f70e-5b53-af4b-3bf056bd41ce" "step-febb20a8-7bec-598d-9521-3df7ff50a618"] :activity/first-step "step-8cc0e099-5714-599b-80b4-eb693886b0be" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8cc0e099-5714-599b-80b4-eb693886b0be" :step/id #uuid "8cc0e099-5714-599b-80b4-eb693886b0be" :step/content "question-d6a9fa51-d96f-5308-9675-af7e9df7f105" :step/next "step-0fcd4859-f70e-5b53-af4b-3bf056bd41ce" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0fcd4859-f70e-5b53-af4b-3bf056bd41ce" :step/id #uuid "0fcd4859-f70e-5b53-af4b-3bf056bd41ce" :step/content "question-ab532852-8985-56d4-9487-9412ea181516" :step/next "step-febb20a8-7bec-598d-9521-3df7ff50a618" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-febb20a8-7bec-598d-9521-3df7ff50a618" :step/id #uuid "febb20a8-7bec-598d-9521-3df7ff50a618" :step/content "question-c989ddc2-999c-5079-ab1b-dc05c9512624" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186162603 :question/answer-fields 17592186160910] {:db/id "activity-e8bff054-dda8-555c-88cb-c434ecb5f2f5" :activity/id #uuid "e8bff054-dda8-555c-88cb-c434ecb5f2f5" :activity/title "Change of Variables in Quadratic Forms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048300 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-d4152a7a-e248-52d2-ad02-b7b482c5a91e" "step-364480f3-7505-5086-9537-4c177a2685d4" "step-78a09b4f-e453-581b-87df-00053d9228ff" "step-2356820b-ea13-5b1f-9c6d-71a0eb74b5d9" "step-e80e0650-b373-5c35-baf3-e32645bedb71"] :activity/first-step "step-d4152a7a-e248-52d2-ad02-b7b482c5a91e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4152a7a-e248-52d2-ad02-b7b482c5a91e" :step/id #uuid "d4152a7a-e248-52d2-ad02-b7b482c5a91e" :step/content 17592186162603 :step/next "step-364480f3-7505-5086-9537-4c177a2685d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-364480f3-7505-5086-9537-4c177a2685d4" :step/id #uuid "364480f3-7505-5086-9537-4c177a2685d4" :step/content 17592186357680 :step/next "step-78a09b4f-e453-581b-87df-00053d9228ff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-78a09b4f-e453-581b-87df-00053d9228ff" :step/id #uuid "78a09b4f-e453-581b-87df-00053d9228ff" :step/content 17592186394915 :step/next "step-2356820b-ea13-5b1f-9c6d-71a0eb74b5d9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2356820b-ea13-5b1f-9c6d-71a0eb74b5d9" :step/id #uuid "2356820b-ea13-5b1f-9c6d-71a0eb74b5d9" :step/content 17592186357686 :step/next "step-e80e0650-b373-5c35-baf3-e32645bedb71" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e80e0650-b373-5c35-baf3-e32645bedb71" :step/id #uuid "e80e0650-b373-5c35-baf3-e32645bedb71" :step/content 17592186272176 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d59c0884-c058-5785-9ee6-42436f91acb4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d59c0884-c058-5785-9ee6-42436f91acb4" :question/id #uuid "d59c0884-c058-5785-9ee6-42436f91acb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-166754" :question/problem "The slope of the line is $m\\,=\\,${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Note that the line passes through the points $(0,960)$ and $(16,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,960)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(16,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-960}{16-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-960}{16} \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=-60.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb014479-3c70-5164-8727-0d40fa526e4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb014479-3c70-5164-8727-0d40fa526e4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb014479-3c70-5164-8727-0d40fa526e4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3c58c900-8ec1-5326-9ef6-6af62d605164" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c58c900-8ec1-5326-9ef6-6af62d605164"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c58c900-8ec1-5326-9ef6-6af62d605164" :answer/id #uuid "3c58c900-8ec1-5326-9ef6-6af62d605164" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176030 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a8749a36-d229-5422-be78-2c6cc7c08abc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8749a36-d229-5422-be78-2c6cc7c08abc" :question/id #uuid "a8749a36-d229-5422-be78-2c6cc7c08abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-166755" :question/problem "Mary covered a distance of $960$ meters in $16$ minutes. Then, Mary's speed was{{field-1}} meters per minute." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per minute, we divide the number of meters, $960,$ by the number of minutes, $16.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{960}{16} & =\\frac{960÷8}{16÷8} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{2} \\\\  & =120÷2 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary's speed was $60$ meters per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70559305-87b6-5c01-98a4-33707a6a0712"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70559305-87b6-5c01-98a4-33707a6a0712" :answer-field/id #uuid "70559305-87b6-5c01-98a4-33707a6a0712" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dc3479d0-1eaf-547f-b2bd-08b36cd460be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc3479d0-1eaf-547f-b2bd-08b36cd460be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc3479d0-1eaf-547f-b2bd-08b36cd460be" :answer/id #uuid "dc3479d0-1eaf-547f-b2bd-08b36cd460be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110744 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a6b0d11-b6de-598d-ac31-b89f5088f71e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a6b0d11-b6de-598d-ac31-b89f5088f71e" :question/id #uuid "5a6b0d11-b6de-598d-ac31-b89f5088f71e" :question/math-academy-id "q-166756" :question/problem "The road between Mary's home and the community park is straight. What is the distance between Mary's home and the point halfway between Mary's home and the community park?\n\nThe distance between Mary's home and the halfway point is$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$meters." :question/worked-solution "![](images/d0/d06fbf44c15301b9fc764823eb6d51652d9fe9426b5aa01b764e4b409d9dc6d5.png)\n\n \n\nLet $H$ be Mary's home (located at $x=0\\,\\text{m}$) and let $P$ be the community park (located at $x=960\\,\\text{m}.$)\n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$ between Mary's home and the community park, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+960}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{960}{2} \\\\  & =480.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8b/8bba4fb81dc0a1e303a1f2bbe5e9d02fe159dfac83f29153401a2e7fda0b8df0.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the point that lies halfway between Mary's home and the community park is $480\\,\\text{m}$ from Mary's house." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-edaa4585-008d-5c7f-88a0-e85d4d9cf19c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-edaa4585-008d-5c7f-88a0-e85d4d9cf19c" :answer-field/id #uuid "edaa4585-008d-5c7f-88a0-e85d4d9cf19c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-922a56af-1c91-50b2-b24b-9200d38a25a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-922a56af-1c91-50b2-b24b-9200d38a25a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-922a56af-1c91-50b2-b24b-9200d38a25a9" :answer/id #uuid "922a56af-1c91-50b2-b24b-9200d38a25a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "480" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054654 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a524e974-5d6b-572b-94df-d3f5d29063a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a524e974-5d6b-572b-94df-d3f5d29063a3" :question/id #uuid "a524e974-5d6b-572b-94df-d3f5d29063a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-166757" :question/problem "The equation that describes Mary's distance from home is $d=960-60t.$ Hence, Mary reaches the midpoint $M$ after$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "Since the midpoint is located at $d=480$, we need to solve $960-60t=480.$\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $960$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}960-60t & =480 \\\\ 960-60t-960 & =480-960 \\\\ -60t+0 & =-480 \\\\ -60t & =-480\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-60:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-60t & =-480 \\\\ \\frac{-60t}{-60} & =\\frac{-480}{-60} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-60}t}{\\cancel{-60}} & =8 \\\\ t & =8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary reaches the halfway point after $8$ minutes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0707692a-470d-5321-afe9-e18fdd3816e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0707692a-470d-5321-afe9-e18fdd3816e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "0707692a-470d-5321-afe9-e18fdd3816e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f35eebd4-15a5-5873-ad46-242b5449f741" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f35eebd4-15a5-5873-ad46-242b5449f741"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f35eebd4-15a5-5873-ad46-242b5449f741" :answer/id #uuid "f35eebd4-15a5-5873-ad46-242b5449f741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138429 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-31feda6f-3ad0-51f3-97d6-60332a952f6f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-31feda6f-3ad0-51f3-97d6-60332a952f6f" :question/id #uuid "31feda6f-3ad0-51f3-97d6-60332a952f6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-166758" :question/problem "![](images/ba/ba84a222a38abb930dbf0dde24479abcbfb3ccdca4f50beec0792e90e212d0b0.png)\n\nSam left home to go to the community park at the same time that Mary left the community park to go home. Both Mary's and Sam's distances from home are shown in the graph above. Based on the graph, we conclude that:\n\nMary and Sam met$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes since they both started moving.\n\nThey met at a distance of$\\,$ \n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from their home." :question/worked-solution "Mary and Sam meet when they are at the same distance from home. At this moment, their graphs intersect.\n\n![](images/8a/8afd4e9a8374ebe1e35200f6172e7fac9ef6c132d84e532c3ac44c25cb838a0d.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(11,300).$ So, Mary and her brother met $11$ minutes since they started moving at a distance of $300\\,\\text{m}$ away from their home." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fd7db8f-f02c-5c00-bd32-ea001fd44ead" "answer-field-170654d3-95f4-55e1-8660-7a93d542bd84"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fd7db8f-f02c-5c00-bd32-ea001fd44ead" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fd7db8f-f02c-5c00-bd32-ea001fd44ead" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9a00f171-1477-5bc9-bee8-f27d2ea3f5c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a00f171-1477-5bc9-bee8-f27d2ea3f5c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a00f171-1477-5bc9-bee8-f27d2ea3f5c9" :answer/id #uuid "9a00f171-1477-5bc9-bee8-f27d2ea3f5c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-170654d3-95f4-55e1-8660-7a93d542bd84" :answer-field/id #uuid "170654d3-95f4-55e1-8660-7a93d542bd84" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-64f226f7-19a1-573f-8ccc-d603990023f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64f226f7-19a1-573f-8ccc-d603990023f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64f226f7-19a1-573f-8ccc-d603990023f4" :answer/id #uuid "64f226f7-19a1-573f-8ccc-d603990023f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5d896b5e-5f76-50d5-9895-9e0c9b778976"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5d896b5e-5f76-50d5-9895-9e0c9b778976" :question/id #uuid "5d896b5e-5f76-50d5-9895-9e0c9b778976" :question/math-academy-id "q-166759" :question/problem "Using the data from part $5,$ find an **exact** equation of the line for the distance $d$ covered by Sam after $t$ minutes.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $d$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $d$-axis at the origin. So, the $d$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(11,300),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{d}_{2}-{d}_{1}}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{300-0}{11-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{300}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\frac{300}{11}$ and the $d$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\nd=\\frac{300}{11}t\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1c6b487-c9a0-5d15-b100-549714f2ddbb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1c6b487-c9a0-5d15-b100-549714f2ddbb" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c6b487-c9a0-5d15-b100-549714f2ddbb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6b3613fa-1ca5-5cbb-8c25-a1409dfd000d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b3613fa-1ca5-5cbb-8c25-a1409dfd000d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b3613fa-1ca5-5cbb-8c25-a1409dfd000d" :answer/id #uuid "6b3613fa-1ca5-5cbb-8c25-a1409dfd000d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{300}{11}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1f3496f7-56e0-5008-8c00-9a987ff3c119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1f3496f7-56e0-5008-8c00-9a987ff3c119" :question/id #uuid "1f3496f7-56e0-5008-8c00-9a987ff3c119" :question/math-academy-id "q-166760" :question/problem "How long did it take Sam to reach the community park from home? Express your answer as a fraction or a decimal.\n\nIt took Sam$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes to reach the community park" :question/worked-solution "Since the community park is $960$ meters from Sam's home, we need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{11}t=960.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $11$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{300}{11}t & =960 \\\\ 11\\cdot \\frac{300}{11}t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ \\cancel{11}\\cdot \\frac{300}{\\cancel{11}}t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ 300t & =11\\cdot 960\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $300$ to isolate $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}300t & =11\\cdot 960 \\\\ \\frac{300t}{300} & =\\frac{11\\cdot 960}{300} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{300}t}{\\cancel{300}} & =\\frac{11\\cdot 960}{300} \\\\ t & =\\frac{11\\cdot 16\\cdot \\cancel{60}}{5\\cdot \\cancel{60}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{11\\cdot 16}{5} \\\\ t & =\\frac{176}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it took $\\frac{176}{5}=35\\frac{1}{5}$ minutes for Sam to reach the community park." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f00c5744-2f0c-56be-b32e-366a3f1f09f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f00c5744-2f0c-56be-b32e-366a3f1f09f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "f00c5744-2f0c-56be-b32e-366a3f1f09f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-adbb6dca-62f9-57ac-bc98-5f7a5c4db312" :answer-field/choices ["answer-adbb6dca-62f9-57ac-bc98-5f7a5c4db312"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adbb6dca-62f9-57ac-bc98-5f7a5c4db312" :answer/id #uuid "adbb6dca-62f9-57ac-bc98-5f7a5c4db312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{176}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" :question/id #uuid "ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" :question/math-academy-id "q-166761" :question/problem "Mary wonders where and when they'd meet if Sam left home $3.8$ minutes earlier and walked with a speed of $50$ meters per minute. She finds that the distance $d$ from home they'd meet can be modeled using the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ d-50t=190.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time (in minutes) since Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes after Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet at a distance of $\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from home." :question/worked-solution "To solve the given system of linear equations, we will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $d$ adding to both sides of the equation $50t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-50t=190 \\\\ d=190+50t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $d$ with $190+50t$ in the first equation and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ (190+50t)+60t & =960 \\\\ 190+110t & =960 \\\\ 110t & =960-190 \\\\ 110t & =770 \\\\ t & =\\frac{770}{110} \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they would have met after $t=7$ minutes.\n\nIf we substitute $t=7$ into $d=190+50t$, we can find the value of $d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =190+50t \\\\  & =190+50(7) \\\\  & =540\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they meet at a distance of $540$ meters from home." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-163d9f6a-4519-5200-83a3-6d401cb44c91" "answer-field-5d99e451-ff6c-54c5-be9e-d8c096902ab9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-163d9f6a-4519-5200-83a3-6d401cb44c91" :answer-field/id #uuid "163d9f6a-4519-5200-83a3-6d401cb44c91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/id #uuid "1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d99e451-ff6c-54c5-be9e-d8c096902ab9" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d99e451-ff6c-54c5-be9e-d8c096902ab9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/id #uuid "13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "540" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "multistep-0193adbb-a9ed-50c0-8c39-bfe4319c7952" :multistep/id #uuid "0193adbb-a9ed-50c0-8c39-bfe4319c7952" :multistep/context "Mary and her little brother Sam live together. Their house is located $960$ meters from the community park. The following graph shows Mary's distance from home as she walks home from the park.\n\n![](images/73/733489f3198f4b26719b2ad770eae3d965f8f008f4a8171ae67c837af68436e0.png)" :multistep/steps ["step-72162a7a-4fa7-5951-9274-5e2f648f9c73" "step-90df7b35-08f9-5219-955a-9347410e43e9" "step-7368ec56-83d3-5cdc-934b-1e058dae67da" "step-0bdd0386-927d-558d-9807-930f47803e99" "step-c6764a5f-7aec-5ca9-a463-76d8b24f9533" "step-f1478ad7-0bdd-5a21-a700-d1940b5cc0f0" "step-f706ef77-3c61-5f5d-a5ef-2c7d49458de6" "step-69cd4aee-1950-50d7-9c94-0376b1dce32f"] :multistep/first-step "step-72162a7a-4fa7-5951-9274-5e2f648f9c73" :db/ensure [:multistep/validate]} {:db/id "step-72162a7a-4fa7-5951-9274-5e2f648f9c73" :step/id #uuid "72162a7a-4fa7-5951-9274-5e2f648f9c73" :step/content "question-d59c0884-c058-5785-9ee6-42436f91acb4" :step/next "step-90df7b35-08f9-5219-955a-9347410e43e9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-90df7b35-08f9-5219-955a-9347410e43e9" :step/id #uuid "90df7b35-08f9-5219-955a-9347410e43e9" :step/content "question-a8749a36-d229-5422-be78-2c6cc7c08abc" :step/next "step-7368ec56-83d3-5cdc-934b-1e058dae67da" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7368ec56-83d3-5cdc-934b-1e058dae67da" :step/id #uuid "7368ec56-83d3-5cdc-934b-1e058dae67da" :step/content "question-5a6b0d11-b6de-598d-ac31-b89f5088f71e" :step/next "step-0bdd0386-927d-558d-9807-930f47803e99" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0bdd0386-927d-558d-9807-930f47803e99" :step/id #uuid "0bdd0386-927d-558d-9807-930f47803e99" :step/content "question-a524e974-5d6b-572b-94df-d3f5d29063a3" :step/next "step-c6764a5f-7aec-5ca9-a463-76d8b24f9533" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c6764a5f-7aec-5ca9-a463-76d8b24f9533" :step/id #uuid "c6764a5f-7aec-5ca9-a463-76d8b24f9533" :step/content "question-31feda6f-3ad0-51f3-97d6-60332a952f6f" :step/next "step-f1478ad7-0bdd-5a21-a700-d1940b5cc0f0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f1478ad7-0bdd-5a21-a700-d1940b5cc0f0" :step/id #uuid "f1478ad7-0bdd-5a21-a700-d1940b5cc0f0" :step/content "question-5d896b5e-5f76-50d5-9895-9e0c9b778976" :step/next "step-f706ef77-3c61-5f5d-a5ef-2c7d49458de6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f706ef77-3c61-5f5d-a5ef-2c7d49458de6" :step/id #uuid "f706ef77-3c61-5f5d-a5ef-2c7d49458de6" :step/content "question-1f3496f7-56e0-5008-8c00-9a987ff3c119" :step/next "step-69cd4aee-1950-50d7-9c94-0376b1dce32f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-69cd4aee-1950-50d7-9c94-0376b1dce32f" :step/id #uuid "69cd4aee-1950-50d7-9c94-0376b1dce32f" :step/content "question-ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "assigned-problem-8dcaf9fe-4b85-5cb3-9d12-8cc51f2110ab" :assigned-problem/id #uuid "8dcaf9fe-4b85-5cb3-9d12-8cc51f2110ab" :assigned-problem/content "multistep-0193adbb-a9ed-50c0-8c39-bfe4319c7952" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [17592186049061 17592186050943 17592186050476 17592186048673 17592186048678 17592186049716 17592186050532 17592186048826] :db/ensure [:assigned-problem/validate]} {:db/id "activity-568eee46-908e-5a57-ae40-3a225118ca94" :activity/id #uuid "568eee46-908e-5a57-ae40-3a225118ca94" :activity/title "Modeling With Systems of Linear Equations" :activity/type :activity.type/assignment :activity/steps ["step-5dd1df4f-567d-5267-ad8e-a2abbf17fd85"] :activity/first-step "step-5dd1df4f-567d-5267-ad8e-a2abbf17fd85" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5dd1df4f-567d-5267-ad8e-a2abbf17fd85" :step/id #uuid "5dd1df4f-567d-5267-ad8e-a2abbf17fd85" :step/content "assigned-problem-8dcaf9fe-4b85-5cb3-9d12-8cc51f2110ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172049 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fb704702-8992-5802-a3da-c6412351672c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb704702-8992-5802-a3da-c6412351672c" :question/id #uuid "fb704702-8992-5802-a3da-c6412351672c" :question/math-academy-id "q-98337" :question/problem "![](images/50/50a06e9bb2865ea9ce3314700d89de3cd12139dee72ddcf2652fb868e88abbcb.png)\n\nWhich of the curves above is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?" :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve II is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve III is not simple.\n\n- Curve IV is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-49afd403-f908-5a66-b217-f75651a04dff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49afd403-f908-5a66-b217-f75651a04dff" :answer-field/id #uuid "49afd403-f908-5a66-b217-f75651a04dff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68a2c705-93ae-5472-bf5d-03e90b1ec07e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68a2c705-93ae-5472-bf5d-03e90b1ec07e" "answer-aa757c82-e2c2-59f8-a04a-5ac6e32331b2" "answer-376695e9-34fc-5ad5-aa0f-2dbf3cbb6b7c" "answer-874231b5-4a07-561e-878f-93d066c20b5a" "answer-f3841a1b-f405-55cc-ad4a-a34c66eb086e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68a2c705-93ae-5472-bf5d-03e90b1ec07e" :answer/id #uuid "68a2c705-93ae-5472-bf5d-03e90b1ec07e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa757c82-e2c2-59f8-a04a-5ac6e32331b2" :answer/id #uuid "aa757c82-e2c2-59f8-a04a-5ac6e32331b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-376695e9-34fc-5ad5-aa0f-2dbf3cbb6b7c" :answer/id #uuid "376695e9-34fc-5ad5-aa0f-2dbf3cbb6b7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874231b5-4a07-561e-878f-93d066c20b5a" :answer/id #uuid "874231b5-4a07-561e-878f-93d066c20b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3841a1b-f405-55cc-ad4a-a34c66eb086e" :answer/id #uuid "f3841a1b-f405-55cc-ad4a-a34c66eb086e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192753 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6487d2c0-d995-5efa-98e2-2110fb813c4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6487d2c0-d995-5efa-98e2-2110fb813c4e" :question/id #uuid "6487d2c0-d995-5efa-98e2-2110fb813c4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-158455" :question/problem "Compute $P(-1<X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{28}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<1) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{28}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}([\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+(1)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}([\\frac{1}{3}+1]-[-\\frac{1}{3}-1]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{28}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25b205bf-9311-59ed-b707-a4ae58c7b68e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25b205bf-9311-59ed-b707-a4ae58c7b68e" :answer-field/id #uuid "25b205bf-9311-59ed-b707-a4ae58c7b68e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15d8b909-cd88-5396-a3e4-015217208b7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca2ee2e6-f6b2-50ac-81bf-610eca1b4575" "answer-41ecd6aa-d66a-5b26-b453-6eb1d066f99c" "answer-5addda90-5bb8-5856-90d0-53bbb72f42a3" "answer-15d8b909-cd88-5396-a3e4-015217208b7b" "answer-7f50f9e1-dab7-5e4d-9b55-64e931613784"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca2ee2e6-f6b2-50ac-81bf-610eca1b4575" :answer/id #uuid "ca2ee2e6-f6b2-50ac-81bf-610eca1b4575" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ecd6aa-d66a-5b26-b453-6eb1d066f99c" :answer/id #uuid "41ecd6aa-d66a-5b26-b453-6eb1d066f99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5addda90-5bb8-5856-90d0-53bbb72f42a3" :answer/id #uuid "5addda90-5bb8-5856-90d0-53bbb72f42a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15d8b909-cd88-5396-a3e4-015217208b7b" :answer/id #uuid "15d8b909-cd88-5396-a3e4-015217208b7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f50f9e1-dab7-5e4d-9b55-64e931613784" :answer/id #uuid "7f50f9e1-dab7-5e4d-9b55-64e931613784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078496 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ac3ed9ab-9e20-50c1-a2df-d0e7acffd405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ac3ed9ab-9e20-50c1-a2df-d0e7acffd405" :question/id #uuid "ac3ed9ab-9e20-50c1-a2df-d0e7acffd405" :question/math-academy-id "q-90726" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-4.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-2x}$ and ${e}^{-4x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{-6x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ea658b1-8a5c-53c8-b110-9aef693ebefd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ea658b1-8a5c-53c8-b110-9aef693ebefd" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea658b1-8a5c-53c8-b110-9aef693ebefd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d7a6d1e-b67a-5086-8d8e-bc807158948a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96581053-e51a-57c0-91dc-cdedecceb889" "answer-4e1371dc-c00c-5e29-9079-f6bee21cefbf" "answer-eca2abbd-fc58-5d08-8f21-69f9b411e1fe" "answer-3d7a6d1e-b67a-5086-8d8e-bc807158948a" "answer-e52cdcee-ace6-5887-9332-30bbc7af4b46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96581053-e51a-57c0-91dc-cdedecceb889" :answer/id #uuid "96581053-e51a-57c0-91dc-cdedecceb889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e1371dc-c00c-5e29-9079-f6bee21cefbf" :answer/id #uuid "4e1371dc-c00c-5e29-9079-f6bee21cefbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eca2abbd-fc58-5d08-8f21-69f9b411e1fe" :answer/id #uuid "eca2abbd-fc58-5d08-8f21-69f9b411e1fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d7a6d1e-b67a-5086-8d8e-bc807158948a" :answer/id #uuid "3d7a6d1e-b67a-5086-8d8e-bc807158948a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e52cdcee-ace6-5887-9332-30bbc7af4b46" :answer/id #uuid "e52cdcee-ace6-5887-9332-30bbc7af4b46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134395 :question/problem "Find $2det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(A)=1\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=4\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+4det(B)=2\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186132409 :answer-field/correct 17592186132410 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162058 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-14c37ea2-4835-508a-983a-3cccd74633e3" "question-0fdadb20-0f32-5fc9-95d6-7a680685f826"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-14c37ea2-4835-508a-983a-3cccd74633e3" :question/id #uuid "14c37ea2-4835-508a-983a-3cccd74633e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-109088" :question/problem "If $\\text{Var}[X]=1,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[7-\\sqrt{5}X].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7-\\sqrt{5}X] & ={(-\\sqrt{5})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-785cf924-e072-5ada-8477-7761baf60c78"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-785cf924-e072-5ada-8477-7761baf60c78" :answer-field/id #uuid "785cf924-e072-5ada-84