 {:db/id "answer-c1bf0d0c-0d78-53bf-b0b4-bd2184337afa" :answer/id #uuid "c1bf0d0c-0d78-53bf-b0b4-bd2184337afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{35w{z}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d86414c-36e6-5bd6-a246-87ac6cb36791" :answer/id #uuid "7d86414c-36e6-5bd6-a246-87ac6cb36791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{35{w}^{3}z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42392060-7736-5a1f-a7d3-d0a4669ba019" :answer/id #uuid "42392060-7736-5a1f-a7d3-d0a4669ba019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}\\sqrt{35wz}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d17d0de9-c925-52f5-bd49-81ba61ecf89c" :question/id #uuid "d17d0de9-c925-52f5-bd49-81ba61ecf89c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141845" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{16w}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{9{w}^{3}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{16w}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{9{w}^{3}} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{16w\\cdot 9{w}^{3}} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{144{w}^{4}} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{(12{w}^{2})^{2}} & = \\\\ 3|12{w}^{2}| & = \\\\ 3\\cdot |12|\\cdot |{w}^{2}| & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 12\\cdot |{w}^{2}| & = \\\\ 36\\cdot |{w}^{2}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA squared number is always positive or zero, and the absolute value of any positive (or zero) number is itself, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36\\cdot |{w}^{2}| & =36{w}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc0cced4-cb6d-5244-b5cc-9c304fe01b62"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc0cced4-cb6d-5244-b5cc-9c304fe01b62" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc0cced4-cb6d-5244-b5cc-9c304fe01b62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6cadb21d-3925-58c7-91fc-d739ee327c7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78f6ba2e-a044-5c94-85cf-c825a698fcd7" "answer-66d3a962-42e6-57db-9470-e68aab60000d" "answer-6cadb21d-3925-58c7-91fc-d739ee327c7f" "answer-423b0bc1-99df-50d0-bdac-012d5259dc1a" "answer-7bf84e7f-1220-51b8-81a0-06fe76cc54c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78f6ba2e-a044-5c94-85cf-c825a698fcd7" :answer/id #uuid "78f6ba2e-a044-5c94-85cf-c825a698fcd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}{w}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66d3a962-42e6-57db-9470-e68aab60000d" :answer/id #uuid "66d3a962-42e6-57db-9470-e68aab60000d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{w}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cadb21d-3925-58c7-91fc-d739ee327c7f" :answer/id #uuid "6cadb21d-3925-58c7-91fc-d739ee327c7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36{w}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-423b0bc1-99df-50d0-bdac-012d5259dc1a" :answer/id #uuid "423b0bc1-99df-50d0-bdac-012d5259dc1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{w}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bf84e7f-1220-51b8-81a0-06fe76cc54c5" :answer/id #uuid "7bf84e7f-1220-51b8-81a0-06fe76cc54c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}{w}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b57aff47-fce6-506a-bd4c-d85de1a296a5" :question/id #uuid "b57aff47-fce6-506a-bd4c-d85de1a296a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-110957" :question/problem "If $z\\ge 0,$ then $\\sqrt{3z}\\cdot \\sqrt{5{z}^{6}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3z}\\cdot \\sqrt{5{z}^{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3z\\cdot 5{z}^{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{z}^{6}\\cdot 15z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{({z}^{3})}^{2}\\cdot 15z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{({z}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & = \\\\ |{z}^{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & = \\\\ |z{|}^{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & =\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z\\ge 0,$ we have $|z|=z,$ and we can simplify further. Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n|z{|}^{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z}={z}^{3}\\sqrt{15z}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5505afd0-bf5c-53e8-aefd-6b87f5951abf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5505afd0-bf5c-53e8-aefd-6b87f5951abf" :answer-field/id #uuid "5505afd0-bf5c-53e8-aefd-6b87f5951abf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-492dabbf-4621-5e6f-9294-dfbe3cbd667e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f0a6e86-1cc6-5082-a1e5-5f66102b512a" "answer-05cd87b2-a486-59e8-85ee-e76c7c31902b" "answer-10e1544e-48e2-5db7-a5cf-be0b233078c7" "answer-492dabbf-4621-5e6f-9294-dfbe3cbd667e" "answer-ddeb8158-e099-5e92-b52e-6505d13a382f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f0a6e86-1cc6-5082-a1e5-5f66102b512a" :answer/id #uuid "9f0a6e86-1cc6-5082-a1e5-5f66102b512a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15{z}^{3}\\sqrt{z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05cd87b2-a486-59e8-85ee-e76c7c31902b" :answer/id #uuid "05cd87b2-a486-59e8-85ee-e76c7c31902b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15{z}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10e1544e-48e2-5db7-a5cf-be0b233078c7" :answer/id #uuid "10e1544e-48e2-5db7-a5cf-be0b233078c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}\\sqrt{15z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-492dabbf-4621-5e6f-9294-dfbe3cbd667e" :answer/id #uuid "492dabbf-4621-5e6f-9294-dfbe3cbd667e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{3}\\sqrt{15z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddeb8158-e099-5e92-b52e-6505d13a382f" :answer/id #uuid "ddeb8158-e099-5e92-b52e-6505d13a382f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{4}\\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-750745d7-1de9-5ab2-9a88-105542b1b50e" :question/id #uuid "750745d7-1de9-5ab2-9a88-105542b1b50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-141931" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{2A}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{5B}=$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the product rule for radicals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{2A}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{5B} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{2A\\cdot 5B} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{10AB}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea0b42d9-2a25-5586-bae6-6fb4cdf2440d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea0b42d9-2a25-5586-bae6-6fb4cdf2440d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0b42d9-2a25-5586-bae6-6fb4cdf2440d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ca4d688c-4249-5044-95cd-38eb34c1e7ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1b3d433-a29b-5881-8391-eb5774e8fd89" "answer-1f45291e-26c4-5a77-a250-9b4d7159788c" "answer-ca4d688c-4249-5044-95cd-38eb34c1e7ba" "answer-b305172d-a42e-5d1a-b232-11e9b4d108e0" "answer-a38e0637-2b88-5e28-aa89-8f04ee007a5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1b3d433-a29b-5881-8391-eb5774e8fd89" :answer/id #uuid "a1b3d433-a29b-5881-8391-eb5774e8fd89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{10+AB}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f45291e-26c4-5a77-a250-9b4d7159788c" :answer/id #uuid "1f45291e-26c4-5a77-a250-9b4d7159788c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{10A+B}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca4d688c-4249-5044-95cd-38eb34c1e7ba" :answer/id #uuid "ca4d688c-4249-5044-95cd-38eb34c1e7ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{10AB}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b305172d-a42e-5d1a-b232-11e9b4d108e0" :answer/id #uuid "b305172d-a42e-5d1a-b232-11e9b4d108e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{20AB}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a38e0637-2b88-5e28-aa89-8f04ee007a5f" :answer/id #uuid "a38e0637-2b88-5e28-aa89-8f04ee007a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{7AB}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b49efc81-0ddf-5a4e-8d55-47ad95f0b7d1" :question/id #uuid "b49efc81-0ddf-5a4e-8d55-47ad95f0b7d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-141846" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{x}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{8{x}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{8{x}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{x\\cdot 8{x}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8\\cdot {x}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(2x)^{3}} & = \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1f83cd6-e452-5786-beb6-ec5bc7114735"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1f83cd6-e452-5786-beb6-ec5bc7114735" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f83cd6-e452-5786-beb6-ec5bc7114735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-293f37f8-650c-59c4-8c5e-887aafb8d3d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f4ac90d-1e90-59c7-8b30-f6f858bde1ec" "answer-293f37f8-650c-59c4-8c5e-887aafb8d3d5" "answer-781dc60c-44ce-5ed6-a636-63ebe0108fe3" "answer-af34ed75-698b-53d3-913f-34e99574be51" "answer-088c6b4c-b361-5d39-9983-8191161ab392"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f4ac90d-1e90-59c7-8b30-f6f858bde1ec" :answer/id #uuid "2f4ac90d-1e90-59c7-8b30-f6f858bde1ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-293f37f8-650c-59c4-8c5e-887aafb8d3d5" :answer/id #uuid "293f37f8-650c-59c4-8c5e-887aafb8d3d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-781dc60c-44ce-5ed6-a636-63ebe0108fe3" :answer/id #uuid "781dc60c-44ce-5ed6-a636-63ebe0108fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af34ed75-698b-53d3-913f-34e99574be51" :answer/id #uuid "af34ed75-698b-53d3-913f-34e99574be51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-088c6b4c-b361-5d39-9983-8191161ab392" :answer/id #uuid "088c6b4c-b361-5d39-9983-8191161ab392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185346 :tutorial/content "The **product rule for radicals** states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\n\t}\n$$\n\nWe can use the product rule to combine radical expressions. \n\nFor example, let's suppose we want to combine the radicals in the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5x} \\cdot \\sqrt{6z}\n$$\n\nTo combine the radicals, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5x}\\cdot \\sqrt{6z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5x\\cdot 6z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{30xz} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185310 :tutorial/content "The product rule for radicals also works for higher-order roots, like the cube root. In the case of the cube root, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{ab} = \\sqrt[3]{a}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{b}.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[n]{ab} = \\sqrt[n]{a}\\cdot \\sqrt[n]{b}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184432 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172047 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-59e59f90-35db-5fb8-beec-b86dd49456dc" "question-da08f493-0f5f-5868-922d-213ef6fbf52a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-59e59f90-35db-5fb8-beec-b86dd49456dc" :question/id #uuid "59e59f90-35db-5fb8-beec-b86dd49456dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-98299" :question/problem "Which of the following curves is simple?" :question/worked-solution "A simple curve is a curve that doesn’t intersect itself anywhere between its endpoints.\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies the definition is the following:\n\n![](images/59/59d3f7eac88247a8c2e1fcf4d0e09b2c28d579b23500ff8e620b4c3dec91ea39.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7a9a4a0-2fea-53c4-88e7-914e96e2af54"] :db/ensur