er-aebbb419-276a-5105-8b5b-cf284740d9ed" :answer/id #uuid "aebbb419-276a-5105-8b5b-cf284740d9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe9e1839-7886-503f-b4a7-91635be110b5" :answer/id #uuid "fe9e1839-7886-503f-b4a7-91635be110b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e08c2f6-3dfa-5bb3-a719-57ef08bb49d7" :answer/id #uuid "5e08c2f6-3dfa-5bb3-a719-57ef08bb49d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13fcbe15-014a-517d-90d2-a926dca99952" :answer/id #uuid "13fcbe15-014a-517d-90d2-a926dca99952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-270268cf-3633-5ce9-82a2-e7b317c9ea4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "270268cf-3633-5ce9-82a2-e7b317c9ea4f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f49b5b4-a291-5bee-8bd7-1b334e3bbe1f" "answer-abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" "answer-f382cd46-5a63-5f00-8839-d2b57a0f4eb1" "answer-7cda832a-8372-5843-9090-ff689f70dcc5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f49b5b4-a291-5bee-8bd7-1b334e3bbe1f" :answer/id #uuid "2f49b5b4-a291-5bee-8bd7-1b334e3bbe1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" :answer/id #uuid "abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f382cd46-5a63-5f00-8839-d2b57a0f4eb1" :answer/id #uuid "f382cd46-5a63-5f00-8839-d2b57a0f4eb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cda832a-8372-5843-9090-ff689f70dcc5" :answer/id #uuid "7cda832a-8372-5843-9090-ff689f70dcc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca23d1f9-e0ba-5c4f-a4c8-1fb3f4fded3f" :question/id #uuid "ca23d1f9-e0ba-5c4f-a4c8-1fb3f4fded3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337398" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y=3x+1.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{2x})}^{′}-2(u{e}^{2x}) & =3x+1 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2u{e}^{2x}-2u{e}^{2x} & =3x+1 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+\\cancel{2u{e}^{2x}}-\\cancel{2u{e}^{2x}} & =3x+1 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{2x} & =3x+1 \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{-2x}(3x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{-2x}(3x+1) \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-2x}(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-2x}(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{2x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-2x}(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{2x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\int {e}^{-2x}(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38566c9c-eb99-5a6b-a9ad-b3ded30c9daa" "answer-field-c479032f-a337-5fcb-94c4-f8162915858d" "answer-field-e8142952-f5ec-5c5e-80de-d77973e116bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38566c9c-eb99-5a6b-a9ad-b3ded30c9daa" :answer-field/id #uuid "38566c9c-eb99-5a6b-a9ad-b3ded30c9daa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b032a7d0-7e3b-558c-b11b-cca85f9404d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5389ae9c-5911-5ab4-91a8-03ab68acf3d8" "answer-1713da84-5fd1-5d91-a845-7d3a35da3e54" "answer-b032a7d0-7e3b-558c-b11b-cca85f9404d4" "answer-e65ebc70-53a8-5cc6-b026-dc7951854da4" "answer-320352c9-552c-5248-98c4-9b92c0952e80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5389ae9c-5911-5ab4-91a8-03ab68acf3d8" :answer/id #uuid "5389ae9c-5911-5ab4-91a8-03ab68acf3d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1713da84-5fd1-5d91-a845-7d3a35da3e54" :answer/id #uuid "1713da84-5fd1-5d91-a845-7d3a35da3e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answe