mplementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-3x})}^{′}+3(u{e}^{-3x}) & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-3u{e}^{-3x}+3u{e}^{-3x} & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{-3x}}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{-3x}} & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x} & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-3x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-920d47b2-3068-590e-abf0-2fae86113747" "answer-field-20ebff2a-086f-5eb7-8db3-ea98b1441d99" "answer-field-ac2790fa-4124-595d-b202-1fbf531eba53"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-920d47b2-3068-590e-abf0-2fae86113747" :answer-field/id #uuid "920d47b2-3068-590e-abf0-2fae86113747" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f80b0984-cac5-5225-97ae-b6ef195606a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f80b0984-cac5-5225-97ae-b6ef195606a3" "answer-363e73c3-14d2-5aca-b3ba-4ef206b7ef08" "answer-fc81d441-b5a7-5ee4-9c97-4238d1d269e7" "answer-732d4a6f-1012-548f-b6da-4987a64f221e" "answer-1161af44-bb89-5c5f-aa0f-dfa35be44438"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f80b0984-cac5-5225-97ae-b6ef195606a3" :answer/id #uuid "f80b0984-cac5-5225-97ae-b6ef195606a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-363