337710" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6640f59d-5879-5651-93ac-a686a27ed14f" "answer-field-db69beff-12cb-5394-9022-20f795e0a42b" "answer-field-e1ca6775-8997-537e-9005-2f0282db799c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6640f59d-5879-5651-93ac-a686a27ed14f" :answer-field/id #uuid "6640f59d-5879-5651-93ac-a686a27ed14f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e2c2cca3-26b7-5eb3-a2ee-91b20eab44ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8584ac2-c71b-571f-b389-5f732c82ff09" "answer-ae932c75-4415-5e10-a98f-aedf2dcc6f18" "answer-a1d04a3f-5d56-51ef-a23b-76cead4b9a67" "answer-e2c2cca3-26b7-5eb3-a2ee-91b20eab44ac" "answer-40348b23-e2a2-5b37-819f-b130a160570a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8584ac2-c71b-571f-b389-5f732c82ff09" :answer/id #uuid "f8584ac2-c71b-571f-b389-5f732c82ff09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae932c75-4415-5e10-a98f-aedf2dcc6f18" :answer/id #uuid "ae932c75-4415-5e10-a98f-aedf2dcc6f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d04a3f-5d56-51ef-a23b-76cead4b9a67" :answer/id #uuid "a1d04a3f-5d56-51ef-a23b-76cead4b9a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2c2cca3-26b7-5eb3-a2ee-91b20eab44ac" :answer/id #uuid "e2c2cca3-26b7-5eb3-a2ee-91b20eab44ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40348b23-e2a2-5b37-819f-b130a160570a" :answer/id #uuid "40348b23-e2a2-5b37-819f-b130a160570a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db69beff-12cb-5394-9022-20f795e0a42b" :answer-field/id #uuid "db69beff-12cb-5394-9022-20f795e0a42b" :answer-field/key